# Data Models & Entities

## Core Entities

### User (`IUserData`, `IMe`)

```typescript
interface IUserData {
  Code: string                    // Unique identifier
  Email: string
  Firstname: string
  Lastname: string
  Phone: string
  Gender: 'MALE' | 'FEMALE'
  NIU: string                     // National ID
  AvatarUrl: string
  Status: 'ACTIVE' | 'PENDING' | 'INACTIVE'
  Profiles: IProfile[]            // Multiple roles
  Address: {
    Code: string
    City: string
    Country: string
    Street: string
  }
  Subscriptions: ISubscription[]
  CreatedAt: string               // ISO date string
  UpdatedAt: string
}
```

### Profile (`IProfile`)

```typescript
interface IProfile {
  Code: string                    // Unique identifier
  UserCode: string                // Foreign key to user
  RoleCode: 'ADMIN' | 'SUPPORT' | 'LANDLORD' | 'MANAGER' | 'RENTER'
  Status: 'ACTIVE' | 'INACTIVE'
  IsActive: 0 | 1                 // Binary flag from API
  CreatedAt: string
  UpdatedAt: string
}
```

**User Roles**:
- `ADMIN` - Full system access
- `SUPPORT` - User verification, support tasks
- `LANDLORD` - Property owner
- `MANAGER` - Manages properties for landlords
- `RENTER` - Tenant looking for properties

### Asset/Property (`AssetData`, `AssetDataDetailed`)

```typescript
interface AssetData {
  Code: string                    // Unique identifier
  Title: string
  Description?: string
  TypeCode: PropertyType
  Price: number
  Currency: string                // e.g., 'USD', 'EUR'
  CoverUrl: string                // Cloudflare R2 URL
  StatusCode: string
  IsActive: 0 | 1
  IsVerified: 0 | 1
  OwnerCode: string               // Foreign key to user
  ParentCode?: string             // For units (references parent property)
  Address: {
    Code: string
    City: string
    Country: string
    Street: string
  }
  BillingItems: string[]          // e.g., ['WATER', 'ELEC', 'RENT']
  CreatedAt: string
  UpdatedAt: string
}

interface AssetDataDetailed extends AssetData {
  Units?: AssetData[]             // For CPLXMOD (complex) type
  owner?: {
    firstName: string
    lastname: string
    email: string
    phone: string
    userCode: string
  }
  Permission: string[]            // User permissions on this asset
}
```

**Property Types**:
```typescript
type PropertyType = 'CPLXMOD' | 'STUDMOD' | 'CHAMMOD' | 'APPART'

// CPLXMOD = Immeuble (Building Complex) - Can contain Units
// STUDMOD = Studio
// CHAMMOD = Chambre (Room)
// APPART = Apartment
```

**Billing Items**:
```typescript
type BillingItem = 'WATER' | 'ELEC' | 'INTERNET' | 'GAS' | 'RENT'

const BILLING_ITEMS = ['WATER', 'ELEC', 'INTERNET', 'GAS', 'RENT'] as const
```

### Contract (`IContract`, `IContractDetail`)

```typescript
interface IContract {
  Code: string
  AssetCode: string
  TenantCode: string              // Foreign key to user
  StartDate: string               // ISO date
  EndDate: string                 // ISO date
  MonthlyRent: number
  Currency: string
  Status: 'ACTIVE' | 'CLOSED'
  Notes?: string
  BillingElements: string[]       // Array of BillingItem codes
  CreatedAt: string
  UpdatedAt: string
}

interface IContractDetail extends IContract {
  tenant: {
    firstName: string
    lastName: string
    email: string
    phone: string
    userCode: string
    address?: {
      City: string
      Country: string
      Street: string
    }
  }
  asset?: AssetData
}
```

### Invoice (`IInvoice`, `IInvoiceForm`)

```typescript
interface IInvoice {
  Code: string
  ContractCode: string            // Foreign key to contract
  StartDate: string
  EndDate: string
  TotalAmount: number
  PaidAmount: number
  Status: 'PENDING' | 'PAID' | 'OVERDUE'
  Notes?: string
  Items: IInvoiceItem[]
  CreatedAt: string
  UpdatedAt: string
}

interface IInvoiceItem {
  Code: string
  InvoiceCode: string
  ItemCode: BillingItem           // WATER, ELEC, etc.
  Amount: number
  IsPaid: boolean
  PaidDate?: string
}

interface IInvoiceForm {
  contractCode: string
  startDate: string
  endDate: string
  notes?: string
  items: {
    itemCode: BillingItem
    amount: string
    isPaid: boolean
    paidDate?: string
  }[]
}
```

### Request/Application (`IApplication`, `IRequest`)

```typescript
interface IApplication {
  Code: string
  TypeCode: string                // Request type
  StatusCode: string
  Description: string
  SubmittedDate: string
  ClosedDate?: string
  IsClosed: 0 | 1
  RenterCode: string              // Foreign key to user
  AssetCode?: string              // Optional - for property-specific requests
  renter: {
    Code: string
    Firstname: string
    Lastname: string
    Email: string
    Phone: string
    AvatarUrl?: string
  }
  CreatedAt: string
  UpdatedAt: string
}
```

### Property Verification (`IPropertyVerification`)

```typescript
interface IPropertyVerification {
  Code?: string
  UserId: string
  AssetCode: string
  Title: string
  Notes?: string
  Body: IVerificationDocument[]
  Status?: 'PENDING' | 'APPROVED' | 'REJECTED'
  CreatedAt?: string
}

interface IVerificationDocument {
  Title: string
  ContentUrl: File | string       // File upload or URL
  Type: VerificationDocumentType
}

type VerificationDocumentType =
  | 'DEED_SALE'
  | 'LAND_TITLE'
  | 'BUILDING_PERMIT'
  | 'DOCUMENT'
  | 'BIRTH_CERTIFICATE'
  | 'INHERITANCE_CERTIFICATE'
```

### Subscription (`ISubscription`)

```typescript
interface ISubscription {
  Code: string
  UserCode: string
  PlanCode: string
  Status: 'ACTIVE' | 'EXPIRED' | 'CANCELLED'
  StartDate: string
  EndDate: string
  CreatedAt: string
  UpdatedAt: string
}
```

## Common Patterns

### Code-based Identifiers

**ALL entities use `Code` (not `id`)**:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
property.Code
user.Code
contract.Code

// ❌ Wrong
property.id
user.id
contract.id
```

### Binary Flags

API returns `0 | 1` for boolean flags:

```typescript
interface Entity {
  IsActive: 0 | 1          // Not boolean
  IsVerified: 0 | 1
  IsClosed: 0 | 1
}

// Convert to boolean when needed
const isActive = property.IsActive === 1
```

### Timestamps

All timestamps are **ISO 8601 strings**:

```typescript
interface Entity {
  CreatedAt: string        // "2024-01-15T10:30:00.000Z"
  UpdatedAt: string
}

// Convert to Date when needed
const createdDate = new Date(entity.CreatedAt)
```

### Status Enums

Common status patterns:

```typescript
// User Status
type UserStatus = 'ACTIVE' | 'PENDING' | 'INACTIVE'

// Contract Status
type ContractStatus = 'ACTIVE' | 'CLOSED'

// Invoice Status
type InvoiceStatus = 'PENDING' | 'PAID' | 'OVERDUE'

// Verification Status
type VerificationStatus = 'PENDING' | 'APPROVED' | 'REJECTED'
```

### Nested Objects

Entities often include nested data:

```typescript
// Instead of just IDs
interface Property {
  OwnerCode: string        // Foreign key
  owner?: {                // Nested owner data
    firstName: string
    lastname: string
    email: string
    phone: string
    userCode: string
  }
}
```

### Arrays of Related Data

```typescript
interface User {
  Profiles: IProfile[]           // User can have multiple roles
  Subscriptions: ISubscription[] // User can have multiple subscriptions
}

interface Property {
  Units?: AssetData[]            // Complex can have multiple units
  BillingItems: string[]         // Property can have multiple billing items
  Permission: string[]           // User can have multiple permissions
}
```

## Form Types vs Data Types

**Separate form types from data types**:

```typescript
// Data type (from API)
interface IProperty {
  Code: string
  Title: string
  Price: number
  IsActive: 0 | 1
}

// Form type (for user input)
interface IPropertyForm {
  title: string
  price: string              // Input as string, convert to number
  isActive: boolean          // Use boolean in forms
}

// Convert form to API data
function formToData(form: IPropertyForm): Partial<IProperty> {
  return {
    Title: form.title,
    Price: Number(form.price),
    IsActive: form.isActive ? 1 : 0
  }
}
```

## Type Guards

Use type guards for runtime checks:

```typescript
function isProperty(obj: unknown): obj is AssetData {
  return (
    typeof obj === 'object' &&
    obj !== null &&
    'Code' in obj &&
    'Title' in obj &&
    'TypeCode' in obj
  )
}

function isUser(obj: unknown): obj is IUserData {
  return (
    typeof obj === 'object' &&
    obj !== null &&
    'Code' in obj &&
    'Email' in obj &&
    'Profiles' in obj
  )
}
```

## Utility Types

Create utility types for common patterns:

```typescript
// Partial update types
type PropertyUpdate = Partial<Omit<AssetData, 'Code' | 'CreatedAt' | 'UpdatedAt'>>

// List response
interface ListResponse<T> {
  data: T[]
  total: number
  page: number
  pageSize: number
}

// Action result
interface ActionResult<T = unknown> {
  success: boolean
  data?: T
  error?: string
}
```

## Key Principles

1. **Use `Code` for IDs** - Not `id`
2. **Binary flags** - `0 | 1`, not boolean
3. **ISO date strings** - Convert to Date when needed
4. **Nested objects** - Not just foreign keys
5. **Separate form types** - From API data types
6. **Type guards** - For runtime validation
7. **Explicit types** - No `any`
8. **Status enums** - Use union types
9. **Arrays for relations** - One-to-many relationships
10. **Consistent naming** - Follow API conventions
